===Etymology===
{{compound|en|draw|back}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈdɹɔːˌbæk/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[disadvantage]]; something that [[detracts]] or [[take away|takes away]].
#: {{ux|en|Poor fuel economy is a common '''drawback''' among larger vehicles.}}
#: {{syn|en|encumbrance|hindrance|nuisance|malefit}}
#: {{ant|en|benefit|advantage|boon}}
# A partial [[refund]] of an [[import]] [[fee]], as when goods are re-exported from the country that collected the fee.
# The [[inhalation]] of a [[lungful]] of smoke from a [[cigarette]].

